# Project Context and Development Guidelines

# This file summarizes key aspects of the 'factorsums' project, its environment,
# and development practices. It is intended to be sourced by .cursorrules to
# provide context to the chat agent and other developers.

# Written by Eric Page with edits and suggestions from the chat agent.

-Tech stack is currently micromamba for project management
--alias for micromamba is set in shell file, should always work as `mm`
---For example "mm activate factorsums" should work
----In fact, chat agent SHOULD ALWAYS run "mm activate factorsums" at the beginning of a session.
----If ever in doubt about the environment, run "mm info" and "mm list"
----Once the environment is active, set up the editable install for local development: `pip install --no-build-isolation --no-deps -e .`
----Note for sage10.6 (which was downloaded with micromamba, as were all other packages) we have pinned python 3.13, even though, 3.14 is released, it is not compatible with sage at the time of writing (June, 25 2024).

*Pickle format (`.pkl`) is generally expected to preserve SageMath object types (e.g., `Integer`) directly upon loading. This has been tested on a limited basis.*

